**Test that the final error is thrown**

No unit test distinguishes the final error from an earlier failed attempt. Add a test with different errors on successive attempts and assert that the last one is thrown:
```js
test('throws the last error after retries fail', async () => {
  const firstError = new Error('first network error');
  const lastError = new Error('last network error');
  jest.spyOn(globalThis, 'fetch')
    .mockRejectedValueOnce(firstError)
    .mockRejectedValueOnce(lastError);
  await expect(fetchWithRetry('https://api.test/items', { retries: 2 })).rejects.toBe(lastError);
});
